Near Chamarel, a river drops about 95 metres over a vertical cliff of basalt into a pool ringed by forest. After heavy rain the falls are at their most powerful, and the spray rises to half their height.

The main viewpoint lies on the road to the Seven Coloured Earths, within the same park, and looks across the gorge to the falls.

## Good to know

- Come after a spell of rain for the fullest falls; in dry periods the flow is much smaller.
- Flying drones near the falls is not allowed.
